Cell[TextData[{
 "A Euclidean head is inert: it holds its points and options and computes \
nothing on its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e01b9be0-60b7-4bc0-a9b5-454143e5db48"],
 " is what evaluates it, reading every property off the head's ",
 StyleBox["graph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] an acyclic directed graph whose source-to-sink chains are \
exactly the head's members \[LongDash] by one forward and one backward sweep \
of a dynamic-programming count, never by enumeration. A circle's graph is a \
",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1b86435-f528-47a9-a14d-0765d19cfe0c"],
 " of necklaces, each ",
 StyleBox["opened",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " at its closing arrow ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " -> ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 ": an acyclic DAG with one source ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " and one sink ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ". A circle's member is the open chain ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " \[Ellipsis] ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " read cyclically, a cyclic vertex list whose first vertex is not repeated."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d161120-7456-43c2-be22-86b901f7aacc"],

Cell["The properties:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c752ecce-2828-4ba7-9ec7-602336734e5b"],

